    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6890" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carsŭlae</span></b> , ārum,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town of Umbria</i>, now <i>Casigliano</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3,
			60</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carsŭlāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, <i>the inhabitants
				of Carsulœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 113</span></i>.—And <i>neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Carsulano (sc. praedio),</span>”
				<i>in an estate near Carsulœ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 1, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
